The Yocto Project is a complex thing, and people eager to get involved=20
can have a difficult time sorting out where to start. The Linux kernel=20
community put together kernelnewbies and kerneljanitors to help people=20
get up to speed and provide them with manageable tasks to get them started.

I think we have (or should have) the "newbies" side of things covered=20
with #yocto #poky and the website and the various manuals and=20
documentation projects, but I think something like "janitors" would be=20
valuable. This could be something as simple as a tag for bugzilla bugs=20
appropriate for newcomers go after.

I imagine this is something we could share with OE - or perhaps OE=20
already has something that serves this purpose - or could be extended to=20
do so.

Thoughts?

